CANARY RUN, PASS A: YOUR CHECKLIST    (written by canary-prepare.sh)
Root @ROOT@
The script answers nothing for you and starts nothing. Four terminals: T1 runs
the script, T2 the daemon (it stays in front until Ctrl-C at step 26), T3 the
console, T4 the second console of step 14 and the integrate command of 20.

BEFORE
 1. sh @PREFLIGHT@ --root @ROOT@
    It must say READY; every FIX line gives the command to type.
 2. qualify-mirror is your own step: set "i_run_this_on_purpose" to true in
    @ROOT@/mirror-qual/config.json, then in @REPO@:
      sh scripts/go-tool.sh build -o build/qualify-mirror \
        ./qualification/leadmirror/cmd/qualify-mirror
      build/qualify-mirror --config @ROOT@/mirror-qual/config.json \
        --out @ROOT@/mirror-qual/report.json
 3. T1: read the dry run, then run:
      sh @RUN@ --pass A --config @CONFIG@ --dry
      sh @RUN@ --pass A --config @CONFIG@ --evidence @EVIDENCE@

AT EACH PROMPT   Enter = go on. A word is typed by you, exactly, and Enter alone
is refused: yes, read, clean. A path prompt shows "(Enter for: PATH)" from
@HINTS@: Enter takes it, a path you type wins, a wrong file is asked again.

STEP  WHAT YOU DO
  1   Lead: yes (no agent session was told about the slice).
  2   Paths of the unit report and the plan summary, then Enter at the rest.
  4   Path of the template review; read; qualify-mirror report path; yes.
  8   Enter (the sandbox inputs file is already written by prepare).
  9   Enter (the stand-in and probe copies are compared with the built ones).
 10   Start the daemon in T2 BEFORE pressing Enter at step 10, wait for the
      listening line, then Enter in T1:
        @BIN@/ataniqd run --canary @CONFIG@
      (The script waits up to a minute for it, but start it first.) Then: yes.
 12   Lead: yes (the probe reported once, every assertion ok except 10).
 14   T3: start the console BEFORE you press Enter at step 14; it waits for
      a ticket (the script mints into the file named here):
        @BIN@/ataniq-console --attach @HOLDER_RUN@ \
          --ticket-file @HOLDER_RUN@/ticket
      Then Enter in T1 (the script mints; a ticket lives 30 s), then yes (the
      pane shows the agent). T4: the same command once more; it must NOT
      attach and only says "waiting for a ticket": quit it (q), then yes.
      T3 is the WRITER: keep its window 100x30 or more, or a paste is dropped.
 17   In T3 give the session pane the focus first (Enter on it; a paste into
      an unfocused console is dropped), then paste the message file the script
      names as ONE paste (do not type it), Enter in the pane once, Enter in T1.
      Paste the file's text (cat it), not T1's lines; "no token": paste again.
 18   yes (the pane shows the stand-in committed).
 20   T4: the integrate command the script prints (with its TIP and DIGEST
      and one --accept-path per path listed); then yes.
 2nd  Second epoch: first close the console in T3 (Ctrl+\ then q); Enter at
      each step; at step 14 start it again in T3 (yes): a read-only VIEWER,
      you only watch, nothing to paste.
 26   Enter; clean (when the evidence holds no login URL or code).
      At step 26 stop the daemon with Ctrl-C first (in T2), then Enter in T1.
      Delete the roots yourself, then Enter in T1:
        rm -rf -- @ROOT@/state @ROOT@/runtime

IF IT FAILS   Stop the daemon with Ctrl-C (T2), answer the clean-up prompts,
  then: sh @RESET@ --root @ROOT@  (type the word reset)
  and run preflight again.
